# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Capacitor native projects.
#
# The native project is COMMITTED, not ignored. `npx cap add android` can
# regenerate a pristine one, but it cannot regenerate the things this chapter
# put into it by hand: the launcher icons at every density, the release signing
# config, and the debug-only network security config. Ignoring `android/`
# wholesale means the next person to clone this repo cannot rebuild the app
# that was submitted to Play — which is the one thing a native project has to
# guarantee.
#
# What IS ignored is everything Gradle derives, plus anything machine- or
# secret-specific.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Gradle build outputs and caches — regenerated by every build.
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/.gradle/
android/captures/
android/.idea/
android/app/src/main/assets/public/
android/app/src/main/assets/capacitor.config.json
android/app/src/main/assets/capacitor.plugins.json

# Machine-specific: points at wherever this machine keeps the Android SDK.
android/local.properties

# SIGNING SECRETS — never commit. See docs in `android/app/build.gradle`.
# The keystore IS the app's identity: anyone holding it can publish an update
# that Play will accept as genuine. It is backed up out-of-band, not in git.
*.keystore
*.jks
android/keystore.properties

# iOS has not been generated; the same rules would apply if it were.
ios/build/
ios/App/Pods/
ios/App/output/
